  "renderer": {
    "selection": "Lookup by kid type ID before selecting the shared body or costume. If a wild type is present, replace ALL shared body/costume layers with its stand body and the shared face. Never draw legacy special props over a wild body.",
    "trim": "Reconstruct authored 256 x 256 orig/trim metadata before positioning; keep the actual GPU texture cropped. Source coordinates, anchors and collision do not refer to cropped PNG dimensions. Use native cropped non-power-of-two allocation, no mipmaps, no duplicate per-instance texture or 256 px flattening. Recheck the 32 MiB ceiling if atlasing is introduced.",
    "appearance": "Preserve saved instance scale. Ignore shared bodyId for wild rendering. Use classic face for new wild births and Dex exemplars; preserve any existing saved faceId of redesigned specials. All four approved faces and all three face states are supported.",
    "transform": "Translate to ground in world; uniform scale = worldCanvasSize / 256 times saved appearance scale. Subtract groundAnchor; apply clip offset equally to body AND face. Face uses its sourcePivot [128,116] at faceAnchorPx. No inherited attachment, shared rig transform, random squash, rotation or second bob.",
    "collision": "Use type lifetimeBoundsPx in place of shared body bounds; transform through the SAME saved scale and groundAnchor as drawing. Keep axis-aligned boxes, gap/overlap contact, continuous/interpolated no-overlap, resolved held preview, free landing and scenery collision rules. Shadows and transient FX remain excluded. Do not migrate saved position without existing free-space reconciliation.",
    "scheduler": "Keep the existing priorities/interruptions. Resolve clips through this sidecar only for these types; fallback is a clip alias, not a request for potato frames. Global phase uses foreground monotonic time. Blink/asleep state overrides the inherited open state; held interrupts sleep. Respawn/return rules remain engine-owned.",
    "effects": "Reuse base rig shared shadow/spawn/fusion/discovery. Rare types only get one existing fx_rare_sparkle sleeve, below all kid silhouettes, per GUI_MVP 16.2. Happy mark remains external. Special-only has no permanent sparkle.",
    "portraits": "Same body+face composition in map, Dex and kid card. At 55 px canvas scale is 55/256. Dex exemplar classic/open, saved live portrait actual face/scale. DOM portrait lists omit sparkle. Do not flatten/cache a different face or add per-type portrait PNGs.",
    "integrationRequired": true
  },
